        "title": "Test Coverage Analysis — canon/web",
        "content": "\n**Current state: 0% coverage.** There are no test files anywhere in the repo (`*.test.ts(x)`, `*.spec.ts(x)`), and no test framework is even installed — `package.json` has no `vitest`/`jest`, no `@testing-library/*`, no `msw`. This is a from-scratch setup, not a gap-filling exercise.\n\n**Recommended stack** (Next.js 16 + App Router + Server Components):\n- **Vitest** — fast, ESM-native, good Next.js support\n- **@testing-library/react** + `@testing-library/jest-dom` — component/hook tests\n- **msw** or manual `vi.stubGlobal('fetch', ...)` — network mocking for `api-client.ts` and `engine.ts`\n- Mock `@/lib/db` (drizzle), `@clerk/nextjs/server`, and `next/navigation` per-test — nothing here should touch a real database or Clerk session\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react jsdom @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom @testing-library/user-event\n```\n\n---\n\n",
