      {
        "title": "A. Pure logic — `lib/*.ts` (highest value, zero excuse to skip)",
        "content": "\nThese are dependency-free, deterministic functions. They should be the first thing tested — cheapest to write, highest bug-catching ratio.\n\n| File | Untested exports | Key edge cases missed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lib/diff-chars.ts` | `diffSegments` | equal strings, disjoint strings (no shared prefix/suffix), one is prefix of other, empty string vs non-empty, overlapping prefix/suffix (`\"aa\"` vs `\"a\"`), unicode |\n| `lib/format.ts` | `shortRunId`, `formatElapsed`, `formatCount`, `formatStat`, `formatClockTime`, `formatTimestamp`, `formatRelative`, `formatConfidence` | `formatElapsed` hour rollover & negative ms; `formatRelative` boundaries at 60s/60m/24h; `formatStat(null)` vs `(0)`; `formatConfidence` rounding (`0.005` → `\"0.01\"`?) |\n| `lib/reviewer-label.ts` | `reviewerLabel` | `user === null`, username null but email present, both null (fallback), empty-string username |\n| `lib/rule-trace.ts` | `deriveRuleTrace` | no resolution yet; rule decided + value; rule decided + no value; no rule matched + proposed value; no rule matched + no value (pure escalate) |\n| `lib/uuid.ts` | `isUuid` | valid v4, uppercase hex, wrong segment lengths, missing hyphens, trailing whitespace |\n| `lib/validate-value.ts` | `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue`, `observedValues` | multiple stacked suffixes (`\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\"`), value *equal to* a suffix (`\"Ltd\"` alone), punctuation-only diffs, both sides empty, candidate matches via folding not exact match |\n| `lib/audit-detail.ts` | `auditDetailParts`, `auditDetailLine`, `auditNote` | every optional detail key present/absent in combination; `from === to` (no arrow); `count` with unmapped `AuditAction` (no noun); `previousStatus` underscore→hyphen |\n| `lib/api-client.ts` | `postJson`, `patchJson` | `fetch` throws (offline); non-OK with `error` field; non-OK with no body; response body not valid JSON |\n| `lib/cn.ts` | `cn` | conflicting Tailwind classes actually merge (not just concatenate) |\n\n**Skeleton — `lib/validate-value.test.ts`** (most logic-dense file, worth the fullest example):\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues, LEGAL_SUFFIXES } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"lowercases, strips punctuation, collapses whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME INC\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips a legal suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Inc\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips stacked suffixes longest-first (pvt ltd, not ltd alone)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not strip when the whole value IS the suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles empty and whitespace-only input\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"   \")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"\", [\"ACME\"])).toEqual({ ok: false, reason: expect.any(String) });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when neither side holds a value (orphan-orphan)\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACME\", [\"\", \" \"])).toMatchObject({ ok: false });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACME\", [\"ACME\", \"Acme Inc.\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACME\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a folded/normalized match\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"acme\", [\"Acme Inc.\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects an invented value not present on either side\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"Nobody Corp\", [\"ACME\", \"Acme Inc.\"]);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blanks\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [\"X\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\" \"] } })).toEqual([\"X\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Skeleton — `lib/api-client.test.ts`** (error-handling focus):\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { postJson, patchJson } from \"@/lib/api-client\";\n\nafterEach(() => vi.unstubAllGlobals());\n\ndescribe(\"postJson / patchJson\", () => {\n  it(\"returns ok:true with parsed data on 200\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      new Response(JSON.stringify({ id: \"1\" }), { status: 200 }),\n    ));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", { a: 1 });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, data: { id: \"1\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"surfaces the server error field on non-OK\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: \"Bad thing\", issues: { field: \"x\" } }), { status: 400 }),\n    ));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, message: \"Bad thing\", issues: { field: \"x\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to a status-based message when body has no error field\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"\", { status: 500 })));\n    const result = await patchJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result).toMatchObject({ ok: false, message: expect.stringContaining(\"500\") });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles a network failure (fetch throws)\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new TypeError(\"network down\")));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles a non-JSON response body\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"<html>\", { status: 200 })));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    // payload becomes null via .catch — confirm this doesn't throw\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
